/-!
# S9-C3h148a: action-normalized Einstein--Cartan spin contorsion

This module isolates the finite representation morphism used by the
Einstein--Cartan connection dynamics:

```text
actual Dirac representation action
→ Lorentz spin covector
→ action-normalized contorsion coordinates.
```

The contorsion map is a direct field update.  Its fixed coefficients are
validated against the existing gravity-BF action on an identity-coframe,
simple-`B` mouth.  The validation comes after the map is defined and proves
that the generated connection cancels the supplied spin covector in every
Lorentz one-form direction.

No residual, endpoint, preimage, range witness, quotient representative,
source coefficient, branch selector, or stationarity receipt is accepted by
the constructor.  In particular, this module does not import the historical
C3h108--C3h120 response/principal-inverse development.
-/

namespace
  SaturationMonoid.PhysicsCore.StageNineEinsteinCartanSpinContorsionAction

